  "blurb": "Working satellites in orbit at each year-end, credited to the owner's country. For decades this was a two-power board of a few hundred Soviet and American spacecraft; then SpaceX began launching Starlink in 2019 and one company now flies about two-thirds of every active satellite on Earth.",
